   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Qwen-Image-Layered splits one picture into separate transparent layers (PNG with alpha), so you can move, recolour or delete one part without touching the rest. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Picture**: the picture to split. Posters, product shots and clear subject-on-background pictures split best.\n   - **Describe the whole picture** (optional): one or two sentences about everything in it, also parts that are hidden. Empty by default; it does not choose what goes on which layer.\n   - **Layers** (2): how many layers you get back. More layers = longer run.\n   - **Long side** (640 px): the authors' recommended size. 1024 is their high-res setting, slower.\n   - **Steps** (20) and **CFG** (2.5): the template's values. The authors use 50 / 4 (more than twice the time).\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 24112026. Type a new number for a different split; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note.\n3. **Picture + description**: nothing to change.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / simple, from the template.\n5. **Split into layers**: nothing to change (see the note there).\n6. Press **Run**. The **Layers** node saves one PNG per layer to `output/Qwen-Image-Layered/`, bottom layer first.\n\n**What to expect:** a 640x424 picture split into 2 layers took 78 s on a 24 GB card (83 s in a 12 GiB VRAM budget, 87 s in 10 GiB); 4 layers of a 640x352 picture took 102 s (106 / 110 s). Layer 1 is the background with the subject removed and filled in; the stacked layers give the picture back.\nA different split? Change the seed or the number of layers. An empty description gave a very similar split here (85 s).\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3, RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 24 Nov 2026 (both README samples, also inside 12 and 10 GiB VRAM budgets).\n"
   ]
  },
